{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-128309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-128309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =-2|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(4-0)-1(1-0)-1(-3-20) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-23) \\\\  & =-8-1-23 \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-128309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "226750f8251e509be463671ba78f03a950cc0fee6988f2255a6404ddf708f85a"} {"question" "q-128309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-128309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-32"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-128309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-32"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-280393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $Q=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(Q)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-280393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3)+2(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))+5(4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =3(2)+2(8)+5(12+1) \\\\  & =6+16+5(13) \\\\  & =6+16+65 \\\\  & =87\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12c467d188bc5b2a0457ffefacb026e2dbc1935b92f38b793f2def9924bf101"} {"question" "q-280393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course